Experimental setup:
\begin{itemize}
\item Training protocol: We fine-tune multilingual transformer encoders on labeled postings and annual-report snippets with an 80/10/10 train/validation/test split stratified by year and industry to avoid leakage.
\item Hyperparameters: Learning rates tuned over a logarithmic grid; dropout and class weights tuned via validation F1; early stopping on validation loss with patience.
\item Fairness and bias: We track precision/recall by province, industry, and SOE status to detect disparate error rates. If gaps exceed 5 pp, we rebalance training data and adjust decision thresholds by subgroup.
\item Computational complexity: Inference cost scales linearly with the number of documents. With batch size $B$ and sequence length $L$, per-batch complexity is $O(L^2)$ for transformer attention; we cap $L$ and employ document truncation to maintain tractability. Yearly updates amortize cost through incremental retraining.
\end{itemize}

\section{Identification Strategy and Methodology}
We exploit two national policy shocks: 2017 AI Plan and 2023 Generative AI Measures \cite{StateCouncil2017,CAC2023}. We estimate dynamic treatment effects using staggered DiD.

Baseline two-way fixed effects (TWFE):
\begin{equation}
Y_{it} = \beta A_{it} + \alpha_i + \gamma_t + \mathbf{X}_{it}'\delta + \varepsilon_{it},
\label{eq:twfe}
\end{equation}
where $Y_{it}\in\{\ln \text{TFP}, \text{ROIC}, \text{Margin}\}$, $\alpha_i$ firm fixed effects, $\gamma_t$ year fixed effects, and $\mathbf{X}_{it}$ controls (industry trends, SOE, leverage, R\&D, IT capital intensity). We also implement Sun--Abraham and Callaway--Sant'Anna estimators to avoid bias from treatment heterogeneity \cite{SunAbraham2021,CallawaySantanna2021}.

TFP is estimated via proxy-based production functions: Olley--Pakes \cite{OlleyPakes1996}, Levinsohn--Petrin \cite{LevinsohnPetrin2003}, Ackerberg--Caves--Frazer \cite{AckerbergCavesFrazer2015}, with Wooldridge's \cite{Wooldridge2009} moment estimator as benchmark. The preferred $\ln \text{TFP}_{it}$ aggregates common signal across estimators.

Instrumental variables: To address endogeneity of $A_{it}$, we instrument shifts in adoption around policy changes with pre-policy provincial infrastructure (data centers, 5G) interacted with industry AI intensity \cite{MIIT2022}, reporting first-stage $F$-statistics and overidentification tests.

Event study:
\begin{equation}
Y_{it} = \sum_{k\neq -1} \theta_k \left(A_{it}\cdot \mathbf{1}\{t-T_0 = k\}\right) + \alpha_i + \gamma_t + \varepsilon_{it},
\end{equation}
with $T_0=2017$ centered; $\theta_{-1}$ omitted. Parallel pre-trends are assessed via joint $F$-tests.

