\section{Conclusion}
This paper constructs a firm-level AI adoption index for Chinese listed companies using patents, job postings, and supplier disclosures. Exploiting policy shocks in 2017 and 2023, we find that AI adoption causally increases TFP by approximately 3.5 log points, ROIC by 1.2 percentage points, and operating margins by 1.1 percentage points. In asset pricing, an AI adoption factor earns significant alphas beyond standard models, with approximately 32 basis points per month and a Sharpe ratio near 0.7. These findings suggest AI adoption represents both a productivity enhancement and a priced characteristic in Chinese equity markets.

